The beginnig of my journey was pretty hard, as my max hp 
was growing pretty slowly as I was gaining exp levels.  
I met many nasty monsters on first few levels and I had to 
pray several times to get myself out of danger.  Things 
started going the right way when I fell through a trap door 
right into a shop and landed on a magic lamp.  I got a wish, 
and, feeling lucky that day, I wished for a +5 gray dragon 
scale mail.  I got what I wanted and my AC dropped to -4.  
I love that feeling!  
   Feeling more confident, I went for gnomish town, hoping 
for another magic lamp.  I didn't find one, but I got out 
of the mines with AC around -10.  My next stop was at an altar 
on level 1, and it turned out to be a quite long, as the 
desired Grayswandir (my favorite weapon) didn't want to apear.  
Quetzalcoatl first tried to bribe me with Demonbane, by I 
kept sacrificing and finally got what I wanted.  Wearing my 
favorite armor and holding my favorite weapon, I descended 
deeper and deeper, finally getting to sokoban.  There I found 
the bag of holding.  
   Also without much trouble I cleared out the rest of the 
gnomish mines.  Having a bunch of unidentified scrolls and 
potions I was really getting desperate on finding a ?oID.  
After one got into my hands (I only found a few of them in 
the whole game), I successfully id-ed a ?oEA.  This achievment, 
connected with the use of one or two magic markers, many blank 
scrolls and some holy water, resulted in my AC decreasing to -22.  
I also discovered that I had three wands of polymorph.  
Feeling that it was becoming my best game ever, I went down 
to medusa, to get my missing reflection.  After that I was 
ready for the quest.
   As I remembered how easily the Minion of Huhetotl perishes 
under Grayswandir, I wasn't expecting anything unusual.  This 
time he tricked me: when his time was almost coming, he read a 
cursed ?oTele and vanished from the quest branch.  I was stunned 
by that and didn't know what to do.  Luckily he didn't get far
and I heard him calling my name (how sweet ;)) on dlvl 6.  
This time he didn't surprise me and died as he was supposed to.  
A magic lamp found in his lair turned into a +5 robe (which came +0).
   Now I wanted to go see Croesus, but unfortunately none of 
the vaults that I entered contained a portal.  So time came 
for the castle.  This caused no trouble and soon I was using 
the wand to get a magic marker, a cursed ?oGeno and some other 
more or less useful stuff.  My AC dropped to -42.  I also made
myself a tame Titan.
   I made a short trip to gehennom where I fought nasties like 
Asmodeus and Juiblex (the first one runnig up and down 
staircases like crazy).  My Titan ate a chameleon corpse and 
happily became a gecko.  He didn't have to kill anymore (lucky him ;)).  
After that, since my max HP was pretty low (about 130),  I went back 
to the castle and used the ?oGeno for nurses (max hp+=130), and wrote
another one for the same use, which raised my HP exactly by as 
much as four (was that _just_ bad luck?).  Anyway, this time 
feeling much safer, I went deep enough to see Rodney with 
telepathy, meanwhile killing Baalzebub, Orcus and Vlad 
(all of them fought like wimps).  
   Scared by the sight of the Grand Wazoo, I headed up to the 
gnomish mines to buy the candles, also making sure that none of 
the staircases heading up were covered by anything.  This was 
a long trip as I couldn't find a staircase somewhere above 
the castle (it was covered by a bugle), and it took me about 3000 
turns before I continued up.  I bought the candles and found that
I had only six of them, so I had to polypipe.  I also discovered the 
missing portal to Ludios, and had some fun with Croesus and the 
Vault Guard.
"Suddenly one of the vault guards enters!"
"Who are you?"
"Croesus"
"Back from the dead, are you?  I'll remedy that!"
So I had to kill him.  Too bad.
   Then I descended those 40 levels,  found the vibrating square 
and searched for a while to find out how Rodney's tower works 
(I couldn't find the ladder ;)).  I finally found him, and he ate 
a beam from the wand of death which I found in the valley.  I went 
down, did the invocation, went down and came back up after a few 
moments with the amulet (not much trouble).  I headed up and soon 
Rodney and the misterious force became a pain in the ass.  After 
a lot of running I finally came all the way up, grabbed my blessed 
orb and arrived at the elemental planes, where I took care of Rodney 
for the last, 14th time.  The orb didn't help me in finding the 
portals, so I wrote some scrolls which did slightly better.  
   Astral plane was a hard fight, but not as hard as I expected.  
With an amulet of life saving on and many !oFH in my bag I felt 
pretty safe when fighting Pestilence and Famine.  Luckily, I didn't 
have to shake hands with Death.

An invisible choir sings, and you are bathed in radiance...
and so on, and so on.
I couldn't copy all that stuff, because I play under Freedos and with tiles.
But there was nothing unusual about my inventory and intrinsics.  I kept
one conduct (genocideless), which I am happy about.

Happy playing to all, I need a rest now ;)

